    <briefdescription>
<para>Helper class to promote a scalar operation to a vector one. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This class is used to move downward extractelement transition. E.g., a = vector_op &lt;2 x i32&gt; b = extractelement &lt;2 x i32&gt; a, i32 0 c = scalar_op b store c</para>
<para>=&gt; a = vector_op &lt;2 x i32&gt; c = vector_op a (equivalent to scalar_op on the related lane)<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>d = extractelement &lt;2 x i32&gt; c, i32 0</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>store d Assuming both extractelement and store can be combine, we get rid of the transition. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
